From 204e7c003441fd5a8c335764ee8093e9bc0714b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 07:40:10 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): one locked, shared GPU device for the trace test
 binaries

trace_composite and trace_parity made a wgpu device in each test, on
parallel test threads, with no lock. A hybrid-GPU Windows laptop ended
both binaries with 0xC0000005.

- headless_gpu now holds the process GPU lock (gpu_guard) and a new
  test_gpu(suite): it takes the lock and gives the one device of the
  process, made once and never dropped.
- The two trace binaries and the view_pass lib test use test_gpu.
- The three ignored evidence renderers take gpu_guard() first.
- egui_app::gpu_test_lock re-exports the lock, so lib tests and the
  shared device take the same one.

Pins: devices_asked_from_many_threads_are_one_device_used_one_at_a_time,
the_trace_binaries_share_one_locked_device, every_gpu_test_takes_the_lock.

Refs #3379
Fixes #3605

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
